            "review_title": "Review at Yoshino Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Charlesquil\nDublin, California305 contributions\n0\nExcellent sashimi but service need to be improved\nMay 2016 • Friends\nFirst time to this Japanese Restaurant (located inside Lotte Hotel) last week.\nThis is kind of high-end restaurant in terms of pricing and location.\nWe have a group of six and ordered 8 or 9-course set menu which is roughly $80/each, including sake (which mistakenly understood each dish will be served with different kind of sake but turned out there was only one champagne-sized glass/each).\nThe dinner started very well with starter and follow by excellent sashimi plate, which is extremely fresh and tasty! Then came a few more dish before we had Wagyu beef, which is also remarkable.\nThe dinner went well until it a disappointed fried rice bowl. This kind of ending is not an ice on the cake and completely off the rail. A little bowl of ramen or udon would have been a lot better.\nAnd finally, the staff, though very attentive but always clean the dish without noticing you've finished eating it or not.\nStill room for improvement to be given 5-star rating.\nRead more\nWritten May 2, 2016",
